<title>FRANCE: Chirac wants VAT cut on multimedia services.</title>
<headline>Chirac wants VAT cut on multimedia services.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac said on Monday he wanted to cut Value Added Tax (VAT) on multimedia services, such as CD-Roms, to 5.6 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;I asked the prime minister and the finance minister to reduce VAT on multimedia services and products like CD-Roms,&quot; he said in a television interview.</p>
<p>He cited a figure of 5.6 percent. The standard rate of VAT (sales tax) in France is 20.6 percent.</p>
<p>This would encourage the development of multimedia products in France, he said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
